# PETEY PLANT — PROJECT LIVING INTERFACE V3
## Consumer Experience, Behavioral Design, Spatial UI & Frontend Engineering

### 01. Your engineering mission

Act as a principal frontend engineer, Apple human interface designer, behavioral product designer, consumer psychology specialist, botanical 3D artist, and accessibility engineer.

Continue the existing Petey Plant application.

Do not create a replacement application.

The previous frontend implementation improved visual structure but remains excessively technical, information-heavy, vertically stretched, and difficult for ordinary plant owners to understand.

Your assignment is to transform Petey Plant into an exceptionally intuitive, emotionally engaging, real-world plant-care companion.

Petey Plant's intelligence should be sophisticated internally and remarkably simple externally.

The application is designed for ordinary people who may have absolutely no knowledge of horticulture, soil science, plant physiology, environmental parameters, or machine learning.

A first-time plant owner should understand the application without reading instructions.

The virtual plant living inside the user's device is the center of the experience.

The existing care engine determines what that plant needs, when it needs attention, and how much water it requires when supported.

Preserve that intelligence. Remove unnecessary interface complexity.

### 02. Non-negotiable product philosophy

Petey Plant is not:

- A horticultural administration dashboard.
- A technical analytics platform.
- A spreadsheet of watering parameters.
- A collection of generic UI cards.
- A virtual pet game disconnected from real plants.
- A chatbot that invents plant-care instructions.

Petey Plant is a living digital companion representing a real plant and communicating meaningful care needs through an intelligent engine.

The ideal user experience is:

Open application → understand plant condition → understand next action → perform appropriate care → receive clear feedback.

The user should not need to interpret raw engine data.

All advanced information must remain accessible without dominating the default experience.

