### 04. Mandatory 60:40 home-screen composition

The mobile home screen must use a 60:40 visual allocation.

60%: Living botanical companion environment.

40%: Intelligent care interaction interface.

The ratio applies to the usable viewport between the compact application header and bottom navigation.

Use a viewport-aware layout with appropriate safe-area handling.

Prefer modern dynamic viewport units with compatible fallbacks.

A conceptual implementation may use CSS Grid with a 3:2 row allocation.

Adapt to the existing frontend architecture.

Requirements:

- The botanical environment must remain visually dominant.
- The primary care recommendation must be visible without unnecessary scrolling.
- The navigation must remain accessible.
- The interface must not clip important text or controls.
- Avoid rigid heights that fail on smaller devices.
- Allow accessible overflow when required by text scaling or exceptional content.
- Urgent care information may override the normal ratio when necessary.

Do not achieve the ratio by making the plant unnecessarily tiny within a large empty scene.

The companion must occupy meaningful visual space.

On desktop, adapt the same principle into an approximately 60% botanical workspace and 40% care inspector where appropriate.

### 05. Home screen information budget

