How much?

Display the engine-supported quantity or range.

If unavailable, display supported qualitative guidance.

When?

Display the supported timing.

How?

Display concise existing care instructions.

Record care:

Provide a clear action for recording the actual amount where supported.

Move unit preferences into this sheet or application settings instead of permanently displaying the mL/fl oz toggle on Home.

Use accessible input controls.

Validate entered quantities.

Do not force users to confirm an amount they do not know.

Do not invent backend persistence fields.

### 20. Smart condition-check experience

Replace lengthy technical assessments with adaptive, ordinary-person questions.

Ask one meaningful question at a time when appropriate.

Examples:

“How does the soil feel?”

- Dry.
- Slightly damp.
- Wet.
- Not sure.

“Does your pot have drainage holes?”

- Yes.
- No.
- Not sure.

“Have you noticed drooping leaves?”

- Yes.
- No.
- Not sure.

Use only questions supported by the existing care workflow.

Implement useful explanations when users do not know how to answer.

Provide simple visual guidance where appropriate.

Do not silently assign unsupported defaults.

Do not require unnecessary questions before every watering action.

Preserve previous valid observations where supported.

Distinguish old observations from new observations.

